1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,800
Setup Tracks gives every track a
General MIDI instrument you can hear.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,086
It reads each track's MIDI to find its
instrument: channel 10 means drums.

3
00:00:13,286 --> 00:00:16,514
Keep the defaults and click "Run".

4
00:00:16,714 --> 00:00:23,443
The first time, the Arachno SoundFont is
converted. This takes a few seconds, once.

5
00:00:25,643 --> 00:00:29,729
The Console lists what
happened on each track.

6
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:36,729
Each track is renamed to its instrument:
MIDI-GPT reads names to know what to write.

7
00:00:39,929 --> 00:00:46,014
Want to check each guess first? Choose
"let me confirm/override each one".

8
00:00:46,214 --> 00:00:51,014
Pick a different instrument
from the list, then "Apply".

9
00:00:53,214 --> 00:00:58,157
"Setup Selected Tracks" works
on the selected tracks only.

10
00:00:58,357 --> 00:01:03,657
Choose "Replace it" to swap an
instrument that's already there.

11
00:01:03,857 --> 00:01:08,157
Using your own synths?
Choose "Track names only".

12
00:01:08,357 --> 00:01:14,157
Everything here can be undone (Cmd+Z
on Mac, Ctrl+Z on Windows/Linux).
